**How to implement.** The app scope is composed over the configured locations, and every test scope over locations under the test output (001 §G; .spec-md §3.9: `AppContext.create` receives every location from settings). The stores stay in memory in this step; step 88 moves them onto the database. (1) `OpticalConstructor.App/AppConfig.fs`: `loadWorkbenchSettings ()` (`AppConfig.fs:136`) becomes `loadWorkbenchSettings () : WorkbenchSettings * DataLocations`. Over the ONE provider it already creates, it reads the four workbench keys as today and the locations through `readDataLocations` (step 82), `install` being `System.AppContext.BaseDirectory` and `documents` `Environment.GetFolderPath Environment.SpecialFolder.MyDocuments`, then saves once. When the file cannot be opened it logs as today and answers `WorkbenchSettings.defaults` with `resolveLocations install (DataLocations.defaultsUnder documents)`, so startup never blocks on configuration. Its doc and the module doc say it reads the locations too. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs`: `create (settings)` becomes `static member create (locations : DataLocations) (settings : WorkbenchSettings) : AppContext`. `experimentExport` writes into `locations.exportsFolder` through `ExperimentExportFile.createCsvFolder` (`ExperimentExportFile.fs:50`) with the clock it has today; the `Environment.GetFolderPath` and `Path.Combine` at `AppContext.fs:110-112` are deleted, because the exports default now lives in `DataLocations.defaultsUnder` (a move). The `experimentExport` field doc names the configured exports folder. No field is added and nothing else changes. (3) `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs`, module `Startup` (`Program.fs:48`, `:59`): `let workbenchSettings, dataLocations = AppConfig.loadWorkbenchSettings ()` and `let context = AppContext.create dataLocations workbenchSettings`; the two docs say so in no more words. (4) Tests. New fixture `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/TestAppScope.fs`, `module TestAppScope` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`, compiled directly after `TestApp.fs`, no comment in the project file. `testLocations (owner : FolderName) : DataLocations` holds `ConnectionString "Data Source=:memory:"` and every folder under `Path.Combine(System.AppContext.BaseDirectory, "TestAppScope", owner.value)` (`Backups`, `Preferences`, `Kits`, `Exports`, `Catalogues`), with `DataLocations.shippedCatalogueDefault` under `System.AppContext.BaseDirectory` as the shipped catalogue. `freshAppContext (owner : FolderName) : AppContext` is `AppContext.create (testLocations owner) WorkbenchSettings.defaults`. Each doc is one line citing .spec-md §3.9. Every test composition goes through them, its owner the test module's name, and keeps its assertions: `AppContextTests` (`freshContext` and the verbatim-settings fact), `LauncherTests` (`freshContext`), `TableAndElementRotationTests`, `WireUiCompositionTests`, `WireUi0040CompositionTests` and `WireUiFinalCompositionTests` (each `AppContext.create WorkbenchSettings.defaults`). `AppContextTests` gains `create writes experiment exports into the configured exports folder`: `testLocations`' `exportsFolder` is emptied first; an `ExportedRun` with one two-point series exported through `freshAppContext`'s `experimentExport` answers `Ok ()` and leaves exactly one `experiment-*.csv` in that folder.

**Acceptance.** After the locations reach the app scope, `AppContext.create` MUST take `(locations : DataLocations) (settings : WorkbenchSettings)` and write exports into `locations.exportsFolder`, `AppContext.fs` MUST NOT call `Environment.GetFolderPath`, and every UI test composition MUST go through `TestAppScope`; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `create writes experiment exports into the configured exports folder`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the eleven s11 invariants MUST pass.
